one way to get around it is to write a function that does RMA but 
reads only the PMs. If you learn R it wont be that
hard. reading only the PMs will reduce the memory use 
by more than 1/2. RMA doesnt use MMs. if you decide to do this, 
email me and ill help as
long as you contribute the final product.

another, less satisfying, way is to run rma by parts (half and half) 
and then join the exprSets.



